[#:seon.task{:name "area-is-contracted"
             :plan "In namespace comp.geo define area [w h] returning w*h, with the Malli contract [:=> [:cat [:int {:min 1}] [:int {:min 1}]] [:int {:min 1}]]. Done when comp.geo/area answers 6 for 2 and 3, refuses -1 with an error value, and carries its contract in :malli/schema metadata. The success test is seon.competency-test/t1-area-is-contracted. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/competency/competency-spec.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "area-is-contracted-typed"
             :plan "Define `comp.geo/area` of a width and a height, answering their product, contracted `[:=> [:cat [:int {:min 1}] [:int {:min 1}]] [:int {:min 1}]]`. Done when `seon.competency-test/t1-area-is-contracted` is green: `(comp.geo/area 2 3)` answers 6, `(comp.geo/area -1 3)` answers the contract's error value, and the Var's metadata holds the contract. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/competency/competency-spec.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "quantity-schema-then-function-prose"
             :plan "Register the schema :comp.order/qty as a positive integer, [:int {:min 1}]. Then in namespace comp.order define double-qty taking one quantity and returning it doubled, with a contract whose input is :comp.order/qty. Done when the registered schema is [:int {:min 1}], double-qty answers 4 for 2 and refuses 0 with an error value. The success test is seon.competency-test/t2-quantity-schema-then-function. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/competency/competency-spec.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "quantity-schema-then-function-typed"
             :plan "Register `:comp.order/qty` as `[:int {:min 1}]` with `seon.schema/register!`, then define `comp.order/double-qty` contracted `[:=> [:cat :comp.order/qty] :int]`, answering its quantity doubled. Done when `seon.competency-test/t2-quantity-schema-then-function` is green: `(seon.schema/schema-definition :comp.order/qty)` answers `[:int {:min 1}]`, `(comp.order/double-qty 2)` answers 4 and `(comp.order/double-qty 0)` answers the contract's error value. Read `seon.schema/schema-definition` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/competency/competency-spec.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "slug-has-a-passing-test-prose"
             :plan "The function comp.text/slug turns a title into a lowercase, dash-separated slug. In namespace comp.text-test write a test named slug-lowercases with at least two assertions about slug, and make it pass. Done when slug-lowercases has run green with two or more passing assertions. The success test is seon.competency-test/t3-slug-has-a-passing-test. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/competency/competency-spec.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "slug-has-a-passing-test-typed"
             :plan "Write the deftest `comp.text-test/slug-lowercases` for `comp.text/slug`, with at least two `clojure.test/is` assertions, and make it pass. Done when `seon.competency-test/t3-slug-has-a-passing-test` is green: the test's recorded run has two or more passes, no failure and no error. Read `clojure.test/deftest` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/competency/competency-spec.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "app-calls-util-through-an-alias-prose"
             :plan "In namespace comp.util define clamp, which keeps an integer within 0 to 10. Then in namespace comp.app, requiring comp.util under the alias u, define bounded, which calls u/clamp. Both functions carry contracts. Done when bounded answers 10, 0 and 7 for 15, -3 and 7 and comp.app's alias u names comp.util. The success test is seon.competency-test/t4-app-calls-util-through-an-alias. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/competency/competency-spec.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "app-calls-util-through-an-alias-typed"
             :plan "Define `comp.util/clamp` contracted `[:=> [:cat :int] :int]`, keeping an integer within 0 to 10, and `comp.app/bounded` with the same contract, in a `comp.app` whose `ns` form requires `comp.util` as `u` and whose body calls `u/clamp`. Done when `seon.competency-test/t4-app-calls-util-through-an-alias` is green: `(mapv comp.app/bounded [15 -3 7])` answers `[10 0 7]` and `(ns-aliases 'comp.app)` maps `u` to `comp.util`. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/competency/competency-spec.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "slug-removes-edge-hyphens"
             :plan "Redefine `comp.text/slug` in place, keeping its contract `[:=> [:cat :string] :string]`: trim whitespace, lowercase, turn each run of whitespace into one hyphen, remove leading and trailing hyphens, keep interior punctuation. Done when `seon.competency-test/t5-slug-removes-edge-hyphens` is green: `(comp.text/slug \"  --Hello   WORLD--  \")` answers `\"hello-world\"`, `\"---\"` answers `\"\"`, `\" a-b \"` answers `\"a-b\"`, `\"\"` answers `\"\"`, and `\"Hello World\"` and `\"  ABC \"` still answer `\"hello-world\"` and `\"abc\"`. Read `clojure.string/lower-case`, `clojure.string/replace`, `clojure.string/trim` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-10/astra-chain-friction.md`."}]
